        "question": "Write a short paragraph on one of the following:\n1. The Lomé Conventions.\n2. Achmad Sukarno.\n3. Typical problems faced by development workers in Africa.\n4. Ho Chi Minh.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "The Lomé Conventions represented a significant attempt to redefine relationships between former European colonial powers and their former colonies after decolonization. Signed in Lomé, Togo, in 1975, with subsequent renewals, the Conventions aimed to establish trade and aid agreements that would benefit developing nations in Africa, the Caribbean, and the Pacific (ACP countries). The original Convention guaranteed ACP states preferential access to European markets and provided financial aid through the European Development Fund, addressing the economic vulnerability of newly independent nations that faced exploitation through unfavorable trade terms. A key innovation was the concept of Stabex, a compensatory mechanism designed to stabilize export revenues for countries dependent on primary commodity exports, which had suffered price fluctuations on world markets. The Conventions also included provisions for industrial cooperation and technical assistance. However, critics argued that the agreements remained paternalistic and perpetuated economic dependency rather than genuine development. While the Conventions demonstrated European willingness to maintain engagement with former colonies on more equitable terms than colonial-era relationships, they reflected ongoing North-South economic imbalances. The framework evolved through successive renewals (Lomé II, III, and IV) as development priorities shifted, but fundamental questions persisted about whether preferential trade and aid could genuinely foster autonomous economic development in newly independent states facing structural poverty and limited industrialization.",
