        "question": "Write a short paragraph on one of the following:\n1. Marshall Aid to Europe.\n2. The Berlin airlift, 1948-1949.\n3. John Lennon.\n4. The impact of the computer.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "The Marshall Plan, formally the European Recovery Program announced by US Secretary of State George Marshall in June 1948, was a comprehensive aid scheme designed to rebuild Western Europe economically and prevent communist expansion. The United States allocated approximately $12.4 billion in grants and loans over four years to participating Western European countries, including Britain, France, West Germany, and Italy. The aid funded industrial reconstruction, agricultural recovery, and infrastructure projects essential to economic revival. Marshall Aid proved highly effective: Western European GDP grew substantially, industrial production recovered to pre-war levels within years, and living standards improved, strengthening democratic institutions and consumer confidence. The programme created economic interdependence and cooperation through mechanisms like the Organisation for European Economic Cooperation (OEEC), which coordinated resource distribution and laid groundwork for future integration. For the United States, Marshall Aid served strategic Cold War interests by creating stable, prosperous allies resistant to Soviet influence and communist parties. The scheme became controversial in the Soviet bloc, where Stalin forbade Eastern European satellites from accepting aid, deepening the division of Europe. By 1952, Marshall Aid ended successfully; Western Europe had recovered economically and remained firmly within the Western sphere, demonstrating that targeted economic assistance could achieve political and security objectives while promoting genuine development and prosperity.",
