        "label": "B",
        "question": "Write a short paragraph on one of the following:\n1. Harry Truman.\n2. The Cuban missile crisis.\n3. Muhammad Ali.\n4. Urban poverty, drugs and crime.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "Harry Truman became the 33rd President of the United States in April 1945 following Franklin D. Roosevelt's death, inheriting leadership during the final stages of World War II. His defining foreign policy was the doctrine of containment, adopted to counter Soviet expansion in Europe and Asia. The Truman Doctrine (1947) committed the US to supporting nations threatened by Soviet or communist aggression, leading to military and economic aid to Greece and Turkey, marking a decisive shift from isolationism to global engagement. Domestically, Truman faced the challenge of reconverting the wartime economy while managing Cold War tensions. He desegregated the armed forces in 1948, a significant step toward civil rights, though progress remained limited. His Fair Deal program proposed expanded social welfare but faced congressional opposition. In foreign policy, Truman approved the Marshall Plan (1948), which provided billions in economic aid to rebuild Western Europe, successfully containing communist influence and stabilising the region. He authorised the Berlin Airlift (1948-49) when Stalin blockaded West Berlin, demonstrating resolve against Soviet pressure. Crucially, Truman made the decision to use atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki in August 1945, ending the Pacific War but raising profound moral questions. His presidency witnessed the start of the Korean War (1950), where he committed US forces to prevent communist North Korean expansion, though this proved costly and unpopular. Truman's approval ratings declined significantly by 1952. Despite controversies, his containment strategy and commitment to collective security through NATO (1949) established the framework for Cold War confrontation that would persist for decades, fundamentally reshaping American foreign policy and global power dynamics.",
