    "parts": [
      {
        "label": "B",
        "question": "Write a short paragraph on one of the following:\n1. Changes in Irish education, 1949-1989.\n2. Ireland and the UN.\n3. Jack Lynch.\n4. Garret FitzGerald.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "Jack Lynch served as Taoiseach from 1966 to 1973 and again from 1977 to 1979, presiding over a period of significant economic and social change in Ireland. His first government saw the implementation of the Second Programme for Economic Expansion (1964–1970), which marked a shift towards export-led growth and industrial development, moving away from the protectionism of earlier decades. Lynch's tenure coincided with the modernisation of Irish society, including increased foreign investment and rising living standards, though unemployment remained a persistent challenge. During his second administration (1977–1979), Lynch's government pursued expansionary fiscal policies, increasing public spending on infrastructure and services. However, this period was marked by mounting inflation and budgetary difficulties that would eventually contribute to economic instability. A defining feature of Lynch's leadership was his cautious approach to the Northern Ireland crisis that erupted in 1969. While he expressed concern for the nationalist minority in the North, he pursued a policy of non-intervention, rejecting calls from more militant elements for direct Irish involvement. This restraint, though controversial domestically, helped prevent escalation into military confrontation with the UK. Lynch also oversaw Ireland's accession to the European Economic Community in 1973, a transformative decision that opened Irish markets to European competition and required significant economic restructuring. His governments demonstrated competent administration during a transitional period in Irish history, balancing economic modernisation with political stability, though the long-term structural problems that emerged in the late 1970s would challenge his successors.",
        "diagram": "",
        "model_source": "ai-h1"
      }
    ]
