        "model": "The fall of the Berlin Wall in November 1989 resulted from mounting pressures within the communist bloc. Poland's Solidarity movement and Hungary's opening of its border with Austria in September 1989 encouraged East Germans to seek escape. Mass demonstrations in East Germany (the Monday Protests) and the weakening of Soviet leader Mikhail Gorbachev's commitment to military intervention under his policies of glasnost and perestroika removed the props of communist rule. On 9 November 1989, confused East German officials announced travel restrictions would be lifted, leading crowds to breach the Wall. The collapse reflected broader systemic failure of communist economies and the absence of Soviet tanks—the instrument that had maintained the Wall since 1961.",
