        "question": "Write a short paragraph on one of the following:\n1. The division of Germany after 1945.\n2. Imre Nagy.\n3. Pope John Paul II.\n4. The impact of the computer on society.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "The division of Germany after 1945 was a direct consequence of the military defeat of Nazi Germany and emerged from decisions made by the Allied powers. At the Yalta Conference in February 1945, Stalin, Roosevelt and Churchill agreed that Germany would be divided into four occupation zones controlled by the Soviet Union, United States, Britain and France. This division reflected the geopolitical reality of the war's end and the strategic interests of the victorious powers. The Soviet zone in the east and the Western zones created a stark contrast in ideology and economic system. In 1949, these divisions hardened into two separate German states: the Federal Republic of Germany (West Germany) aligned with the West, and the German Democratic Republic (East Germany) under Soviet control. West Germany experienced rapid economic recovery through the Marshall Plan and developed as a capitalist democracy, while East Germany became a communist state under Soviet dominance. The division symbolized the broader Cold War split between communist and capitalist blocs in Europe. Berlin, located deep within East Germany but also divided into four zones, became a flashpoint of Cold War tensions, most dramatically illustrated by the construction of the Berlin Wall in 1961 to prevent East Germans fleeing westward. The division of Germany remained one of the most significant consequences of World War II and a defining feature of Cold War Europe until German reunification in 1990 following the collapse of Soviet communism.",
